In 2024, Vietnam&apos;s Mekong Delta surpassed USD 10 billion in seafood exports, solidifying its status as a cold logistics epicenter in Southeast Asia. This rapid growth is not just about volume&#x2014;it reflects a structural shift toward sustainable, tech-enabled supply chains. 

At Logchain Holdings, we view Vietnam as a high-potential market for: 

&#x2705; Foreign direct investment into logistics infrastructure&#xA0;
&#x2705; Joint ventures with local leaders in cold storage&#xA0;
&#x2705; Development of ESG-compliant, solar-powered warehouses&#xA0;
&#x2705; Digitally integrated supply chain management aligned with EU standards&#xA0;
&#x1F4CC; Noteworthy developments: 

Lineage Logistics (USA): Solar-integrated cold storage in Can Tho, reducing energy use by 40%&#xA0;
