On June 27, this iconic dish was officially recognized as a National Intangible Cultural Heritage of Vietnam by the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Loved by both locals and travelers, b&#xFA;n b&#xF2; Hu&#x1EBF; carries deep culinary roots and is often considered a must-try when visiting Central Vietnam.

In 2014, the late Anthony Bourdain featured it on CNN and named it one of the Top 100 Asian Dishes by the Asia Book of Records in 2016. In 2023, TasteAtlas ranked Hu&#x1EBF; among the top 100 food cities in the world, with b&#xFA;n b&#xF2; Hu&#x1EBF; highlighted as a signature dish.

With its fragrant broth infused with lemongrass, shrimp paste, and chili oil, and its unique depth depending on each cook&#x2019;s touch, this dish continues to represent both flavor and tradition, passed down from kitchen to kitchen &#x1F962;

